# Six languages

bonsai's own fixtures, in place: its findings, and how many of them zanity reports on the same lines.

| Smell | python | javascript | typescript | go | rust | java | Note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `dead-parameter` | [3/9]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [3/4]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [6/21]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [10/15]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [7/12]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [4/8]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | bonsai also flags method parameters an interface or override fixes, empty stubs, TypeScript parameter properties, and parameters inside function types; zanity leaves those alone |
| `dead-symbol` | [23/23]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [19/20]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [22/30]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [18/21]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [14/20]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | [18/31]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) | bonsai also flags exported or public members and types still named by signatures or implementations; zanity leaves externally reachable and structurally referenced code alone |
| `duplicated-expression` | [2/2]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [2/2]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [0/1]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) | [1/1]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [1/1]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [–]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | bonsai also flags the same text in separate loops, where each loop binds a different value; zanity reports only an expression it could compute once |
| `empty-handler` | [1/1]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [–]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [–]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [–]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [1/1]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [1/1]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
